From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 14:14:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs(onboarding): surface recall +
 merge/insights/upgrade/gate/role in AGENTS.md and prime

`forge setup` generates a project's AGENTS.md by copying/smart-merging Forge's
own root AGENTS.md, so that file is the canonical onboarding surface new users
and agents read. It told agents to `forge remember` but never `forge recall`
(a write-only memory loop), and never surfaced `forge merge`, `forge insights`,
`forge upgrade`, `forge gate`, or `forge role` (0 mentions).

- AGENTS.md: close the remember/recall loop and add a concise, accurate
  quick-reference line for each previously-invisible command (wording taken
  from each command's real --help).
- lib/orientation.js: add a bounded, preserve:true "Key Commands" section to
  `forge prime` (session entry) so these capabilities are discoverable without
  bloating the token budget; `forge orient` is unchanged.
- test: regression test drives the real `forge setup` CLI against a fresh git
  repo and asserts the generated AGENTS.md surfaces recall + the new commands,
  guarding the gap from returning.

Advances kernel issue 1be54343 (prime.js: embed one-glance orientation block).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
